Instead of jumping in to defend yourself immediately, you could ask calmly, did you mean for that comment to sound rude?

224
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:05,210
Or did you mean to omit my name when you were talking about the success of that project?

225
00:13:05,770 --> 00:13:09,180
Or even did you intend to embarrass me in front of everyone with that remark?

226
00:13:09,220 --> 00:13:09,560
Wow.

227
00:13:09,620 --> 00:13:10,180
Okay.

228
00:13:10,210 --> 00:13:11,930
Those questions really cut through the noise.

229
00:13:11,990 --> 00:13:16,810
They're not phrased like accusations, but they absolutely demand clarity and make the person accountable.

230
00:13:17,250 --> 00:13:19,670
I can totally see using those in a business situation.

231
00:13:19,730 --> 00:13:30,400
Like if you get an email that feels kind of passive aggressive or accusatory, instead of firing back an equally charged email, you could reply, did you mean to imply that I missed the deadline?

232
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:38,050
